<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="set-bonuses">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_treasurechest02b.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Blood Death Knight in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>Compared to other classes, the Blood Death Knight tier bonus in Phase 3 is quite lackluster, but still offers decent utility. For this tier, it's worth looking at both the tank and the DPS tier sets, as we can benefit from both. <br/>
<br/>The tank set is very well itemized for us as Blood Death Knights this time around. The 2-set bonus turns <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=59754/rune-tap">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_runetap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rune Tap</span></a> into an actually usable ability outside of when <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=81164/will-of-the-necropolis">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_creature_cursed_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Will of the Necropolis</span></a> procs and slightly reduces its cooldown. This bonus is not that powerful. The 4-set bonus gives us an additional 90 Runic Power per minute, which equates to 3x <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=56815/rune-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_darkconviction.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rune Strike</span></a> casts. When we're high enough item level to consider equipping the 4-set bonus, resource generation should be high enough to leave you without empty globals; that said, being able to use additional <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=56815/rune-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_darkconviction.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rune Strike</span></a>, rather than using blood runes, will be a net benefit. <br/>
<br/>The DPS set is also very interesting to us in this phase. The 2-set will summon a ghoul-like pet that deals damage to your target for 15 seconds. This pet can also be used for <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48743/death-pact">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_deathpact.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Pact</span></a> if your <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=46584/raise-dead">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_animatedead.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raise Dead</span></a> isn't active and on cooldown. The 4-set is what really makes the set shine, making the execute portion of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=130736/soul-reaper">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_soulreaper.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a> usable from 45% rather than 35%. This is a massive offensive gain and further increases the offensive value of Cinderglacier as a weapon enchant. <br/>
<br/>I'd generally recommend using the DPS set. The tank set falls a bit to the wayside, as tier pieces cannot be upgraded to Thunderforged, meaning you'll gain more offensive and defensive utility by pursuing off-pieces.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="tier-15-dps">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">DPS Tier 15 - <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item-set=1152/battleplate-of-the-all-consuming-maw">
