<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/spell_nature_lightningshield.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Blood Death Knight Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>Your trinket usage will be dictated by what it is that you and your raid need. A Stamina trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96555/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> will make you the least likely to die, especially in a 25-player raiding environment, while a trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96398/spark-of-zandalar">
<img alt="Spark of Zandalar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_lightningshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spark of Zandalar</span></a> will offer avoidance through the high Strength-to-Parry conversion, with some damage and active mitigation through the haste. Trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96915/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> will offer the highest throughput, but very limited defensive utility. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96543/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> - This is by far your strongest offensive trinket, and the more crit you have, the better it performs. Because of our avoidance-to-crit conversion through Riposte, this trinket offers strong utility even in a defensively focused set.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96501/primordius-talisman-of-rage">
<img alt="Primordius' Talisman of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordius' Talisman of Rage</span></a> - This is our second strongest offensive trinket. It does not perform that much better offensively than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96398/spark-of-zandalar">
<img alt="Spark of Zandalar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_lightningshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spark of Zandalar</span></a> and brings little defensive utility. I don't recommend using it unless it's for a strictly offensive set.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> - This is one of the few trinkets in this phase that still has an internal cooldown (ICD), and the ICD of this trinket happens to almost perfectly line up with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>, making it a very strong trinket. The drawback is that it has mainstat expertise, and you'll likely go over the soft-cap, even when reforging away expertise.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96398/spark-of-zandalar">
<img alt="Spark of Zandalar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_lightningshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spark of Zandalar</span></a> - This trinket will be highly in demand, but is a very strong, balanced trinket for the Blood Death Knight. I'd highly recommend picking up this trinket if you're looking to use a more defensive or balanced set.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87172/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> - While Strength and Haste look like offensive stats, this offers the best of both worlds, bringing damage through Strength and Haste while offering defensive utility through the Strength-to-Parry conversion, and faster Rune regeneration from the Haste. A super solid trinket, but it has a long internal cooldown (ICD) and can proc at inopportune moments.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87072/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> - Slightly worse than the options above, but it offers similar utility with Strength and Haste.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=93256/skullrender-medallion">
<img alt="Skullrender Medallion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skullrender Medallion</span></a> - Trinket with limited defensive utility, but offers strong offensive throughput.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96555/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> - This is by far your best defensive trinket in Phase 3 and is realistically the only fully defensive trinket worth considering.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=91210/tyrannical-gladiators-emblem-of-tenacity">
<img alt="Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_endlessrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity</span></a> - The second-best defensive trinket in Phase 3 comes from PVP. This trinket can also be used effectively in fights where you get Vengeance cap in order to extend that cap with the on-use health effect. The trinket's on-use does not share cooldown with other trinkets or tinkers.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> - The 8871 Dodge also translates into solid offensive utility. Like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a>, this trinket will be quite expensive, but less so than the Strength one.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89079/lao-chins-liquid-courage">
<img alt="Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage</span></a> - This trinket has similar defensive utility to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> but only offers defensive utility. Not recommended unless for a specific purpose.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87160/stuff-of-nightmares">
<img alt="Stuff of Nightmares" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stuff of Nightmares</span></a> - This trinket offers less defensive utility than the Stamina counterparts, but does bring more offensive utility through reforging the Mastery and its Dodge proc effect.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87063/vial-of-dragons-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Dragon's Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Dragon's Blood</span></a> - Similar to the above option, just worse.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
